n', allowing for different process variants based on which event (if any) occurs.\",\"template\":\"Not Co-Existence\",\"activation\":{\"name\":\"Submit Application\",\"description\":\"The 'Submit Application' activity represents the initial submission of a flexible work arrangement request, capturing the arrangement type and application ID.\"},\"target\":{\"name\":\"Review Application\",\"description\":\"The 'Review Application' activity involves reviewing a submitted application, recording the application ID, application status, and a review score.\"},\"activation_condition\":null,\"correlation_condition\":null,\"time_condition\":null,\"cardinality\":null},{\"type\":\"binary\",\"description\":\"The 'Approve Application' activity is permitted to occur only if a 'Review Application' activity has occurred before it within the same process instance. 'Approve Application' that occurs without any prior 'Review Application' is a violation of the constraint. Multiple 'Review Application' can occur, and any number of events can happen between a 'Review Application' and a subsequent 'Approve Application'. This ensures that the approval cannot proceed without the necessary review being completed first.\",\"template\":\"Precedence\",\"activation\":{\"name\":\"Approve Application\",\"description\":\"The 'Approve Application' activity represents the approval of a reviewed application, updating the application ID and application status.\"},\"target\":{\"name\":\"Review Application\",\"description\":\"The 'Review Application' activity involves reviewing a submitted application, recording the application ID, application status, and a review score.\"},\"activation_condition\":null,\"correlation_condition\":null,\"time_condition\":null,\"cardinality\":null},{\"type\":\"binary\",\"description\":\"Exactly one of the activities 'Approve Application' or 'Reject Application' must occur in the process instance. This means that the process is compliant if only 'Approve Application' occurs w